VOID(1)                    User Commands                    VOID(1)

NAME
       void - The Void OS hacker training terminal

SYNOPSIS
       void
       void-web

DESCRIPTION
       The Void OS is an ultra-minimalist, poetic, dark interactive
       terminal game for training elite hackers through real Linux
       command simulation.

       Inspired by The Dark Room, Ruby Koans, pwn.college, PicoCTF,
       Hacker 101, OverTheWire, and Phrack Magazine lore.

MODES
       void       CLI mode - runs in terminal
       void-web   Web mode - opens in browser

GAME MODES
       play         Main campaign - 8 levels across 4 tracks
       walkthrough  Guided tutorial, step by step
       riddles      Logic puzzles about hacker history
       hackername   Generate your serial alias

TRACKS
       Track 1: Sensing the Void
           Levels 1.1-1.3: Redirection, hidden files, pipelines

       Track 2: Altering Reality
           Levels 2.1-2.2: PATH hijacking, environment variables

       Track 3: Privilege Escalation
           Levels 3.1-3.2: SUID, cronjob injection

       Track 4: Memory Reversing
           Level 4.1: Buffer overflow

SHELL COMMANDS
       Navigation:
           ls [-la] [path]       List directory
           cd <path>             Change directory
           pwd                   Print working dir
           find [-name x]        Search files

       Files:
           cat <file>            Read file
           echo <text> > file    Write to file
           touch <name>          Create file
           mkdir <name>          Create directory
           chmod <perm> <file>   Change permissions

       Analysis:
           file <file>           Identify file type
           stat <file>           File metadata
           strings <file>        Extract printable strings
           grep <pattern>        Search contents

       Crypto:
           decode <txt> <type>   Decode (base64/hex/rot13)
           caesar <txt> <shift>  Caesar cipher
           hash <txt> [algo]     Hash (md5/sha1/sha256)

       System:
           man <command>         Manual page
           hint                  Get level hint
           submit FLAG{...}      Submit flag

EXAMPLES
       void                    Start the game
       void-web                Start web server

FILES
       ~/.void_os/             Game data directory
       ~/.void_os/void_os.py   Game engine
       ~/.void_state.json      Save file
       ~/.void_history         Command history
       ~/.void_diary.md        Game diary

